messages:
liz_sales: Heads-up — Zenith POC demo today hit streaming issues. Customer saw SSE disconnects + 'Unexpected end of JSON input' in their webview during the summary stream. Demo got interrupted.
mike_se: Ugh. Do we have a request_id or sample logs from their client? Was it during high throughput or a single stream? @aaron_oncall can you watch the cluster logs?
ajosh_customer: (customer) Sending clipped console log and server trace. Client shows repeated partial JSON chunks then parser fails. Happens after ~45s of streaming. We retried and it sometimes works. Logs pasted below.
ajosh_customer: client console: "SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at JSON.parse (<anonymous>) at parseChunk (app.bundle.js:342)"
server: SSE connection closed by client id=zt-73, bytes_sent=2048, keepalive=1
server: write error: broken pipe

mike_se: Can you paste the exact chunk fragments? Need to see whether events are being split across SSE boundaries or the client concat is broken.
ajosh_customer: sample chunk sequence (copied from browser network tab):

-- event: message
data: {"r":1,"text":"Hello

"}

-- event: message
data: {"r":2,"text":"This is a lo

"
-- event: message
data: {"r":2,"text":"ng message continued"}

client then tries JSON.parse on each data payload and fails on the middle one (it was truncated)

aaron_oncall: Looking at infra — I see intermittent keepalive timeouts on the front-proxy for that customer's region around the same time. Also a few 429s from the API gateway for that customer API key, spike at 45s. Proxy logs: "upstream timed out (110): client prematurely closed connection" and nginx: "recv() failed (104: Connection reset by peer)". Could be retry storm + proxy buffering causing odd frame reassembly.
mike_se: That sounds like two problems colliding: (1) client-side parser not tolerant of split JSON across multiple SSE data chunks, and (2) retries/rate limits causing replays/early closes. We should recommend the SDK handle partial frames and also reduce retry aggressiveness.
ci-bot: deployment v2.14.1 rolled to canary in eu-west-1 at 2103006700
liz_sales: Customer also asked about a quick workaround before tomorrow's exec demo. Any safe config we can ask them to apply on their webview or proxy?
mike_se: Short-term: on their webview change parser to accumulate data events until a full JSON object is received (e.g., try/catch JSON.parse and buffer partial strings). Also ask their CDN/proxy to disable response buffering (proxy_buffering off) and increase keepalive_timeout to 90s. That should reduce truncation and premature closes.
aaron_oncall: On our side: I'll throttle back gateway retries for that org to avoid 429 cascades and add a canary config to keep the connection alive longer (increase SSE ping interval and ensure we send heartbeat comments ":
" every 15s). I'll also add metrics to detect partial-event rates.
mike_se: For long-term: recommend SDK change to use an event-stream parser that supports multi-chunk JSON payloads (concatenate data: lines before parse). We can throw an example snippet in the docs.
liz_sales: @josh_customer do you want us to push a temporary patch and a one-off config change? We can do the gateway throttle now.
josh_customer: Yes please — we'll apply the proxy change and accept your gateway throttle. Also can you share the parser snippet? We're using a third-party webview wrapper so patching is slightly painful.
mike_se: Snippet to share: ```js
// simple accumulator for SSE data events
let buffer = ''
function onSSEData(chunk) {
  buffer += chunk;
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(buffer);
    handle(obj);
    buffer = '';
  } catch (e) {
    // still partial — wait for next chunk
  }
}
```
Add a max buffer timeout to avoid memory growth.
aaron_oncall: Actions: (1) infra throttle for org zenith applied (done) (2) keepalive/heartbeat increase on canary (in progress) (3) add metric for partial-parse failures (queued). I'll follow up in #eng-runtime if rollout changes.
liz_sales: Thanks team. I'll coordinate with customer for proxy change and follow up tomorrow morning. Marking as high-priority POC support. :thumbsup:
josh_customer: Thanks all — will try proxy tweak now and report back in ~30m.
